{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Perhaps ten will be found there.</b> Rashi explained: nine, by joining [HaShem's presence to make ten]. He already sought and did not find. And I do not know what is different, that regarding forty-five it is written לא אשחית, and regarding forty and thirty it is written לא אעשה, and then it writes again לא אשחית regarding twenty and ten. Therefore it appears to explain the verses thus: ״ויאמר אברהם אולי ימצאון שם חמשים צדיקים״ — that is, a complete tally for five cities. And the Holy One, blessed be He, answered: ״אם אמצא וגו׳ ונשאתי לכל המקום בעבורם״ — meaning, since it is a complete tally, I will forgive their sin and not destroy them, and also not afflict them with suffering. ״ויאמר אולי יחסרון חמשה״ — that is, nine for each and every city, and You will join with each nine and nine and complete the tally. And the Holy One, blessed be He, answered: לא אשחית אם אמצא שם ארבעים וחמשה — meaning, I will not destroy them, but I will afflict them with suffering, since a complete tally without joining will not be found among them. ״ויאמר אברהם אולי ימצאון שם ארבעים״ — that is, a complete tally for four cities; and likewise for three cities. And the Holy One, blessed be He, said: לא אעשה בעבור הארבעים and לא בעבור השלשים — meaning, I will forgive and not do anything to them — neither destruction nor suffering — since the tally is complete and they will also be the majority of the cities. ״ויאמר אברהם אולי ימצאון שם עשרים״ — that is, a complete tally for two cities, and likewise ten for one city. And the Holy One, blessed be He, said: לא אשחית בעבור העשרים and likewise בעבור העשרה — meaning, I will not destroy them completely, but I will afflict them with suffering, since this will be only the minority of five cities, even though the tally is complete for two or for one. And that is what Rashi explained: regarding nine and joining — Abraham did not ask when he did not find ten, for he had already sought and did not find. And he investigated what the joining would accomplish, and did not find in the words of the Holy One, blessed be He, that joining would atone like a complete tally. And joining saves only from destruction, not from suffering. And some say: for fewer than ten he did not ask, for he thought Lot and his wife and his four daughters and his four sons-in-law — who are ten — would be worthy to save the city on their merit."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:42.851368769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}